# Visor Boot Manager v1.5.2

## Fixes

- Snapshot auto-detection no longer freezes on slow or damaged volumes.
  A per-volume time budget of 8 seconds is enforced, with watchdog kicking
  and progress logging so a hang is attributable to a single volume (#21).

- Password confirmation now uses constant-time comparison, preventing
  timing side-channel attacks against the confirmation field.

- SHA-256 context is zeroed after finalizing, preventing key material
  from lingering on the stack.

- PBKDF2 iteration count below 100,000 is now rejected on decrypt,
  preventing use of weak derivation parameters.

## Improvements

- PNG decoder supports Adam7 interlaced images. Interlaced PNGs (the
  default output of most image editors) now load correctly as backgrounds
  and icons instead of falling back to defaults or failing silently.

- `efi_strlen16()` is the single shared implementation across the
  codebase, replacing three redundant local definitions.

- `mem_equal()` is a public constant-time comparison function, available
  to any module that needs side-channel-resistant equality checks.

- `efi_fread()` simplified: the redundant `size > requested` clamp is
  removed since UEFI `HandleRead` never returns more than requested.

- Snapshot scan logs which volume is being scanned, and reports when no
  snapshots are found on any volume instead of silently continuing.
